                 who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - This looks good. Before finalizing, please overhaul the number tags in l. 12, write &lt;:(δεδηλωμένω(ν))|reg|(δ̣ε̣δ̣η̣λ̣ουμένω(ν)):&gt; in l. 23, and add accents to the irregular forms in lines 25 (ἥδηι, ἔστων) and 26 (ἐπιφερόμενον). </change>
         <change when="2026-10-30T18:07:09+00:00"
                 who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/Bianca%20Borrelli">Submit - Entered BL corrections to ll. 1 and 12 and PN correction to l. 19: πᾶν̣ ἐκπεπτω|κέναι =&gt; παρ̣εκπεπτωκέναι. There is no room for nu. Moreover, πᾶν is unparalleled in this formula; παραπίπτω (less frequently ἐκπίπτω) is the verb normally used to indicate that a document has been lost; the double preverb παρεκ- is found in P.Fam.Tebt. 15.71, where it however is mostly damaged, and in an unpublished papyrus from Tebtynis, PSI inv. 3055 (ed. forthcoming), where it is clearly legible.</change>
